# NORMAL USE: leave VITE_API_TOKEN empty. The console opens a login screen; sign in with a Registration
# test account (SH-S01). Our API checks the password with Registration (authenticate, then validate, as
# Registration's Auth Guide says) and gives the console its own token. Registration's login lasts about
# 15–20 minutes, so you are asked to sign in again after that.
#
# BACKUP ONLY (Registration is down): put a fixed dev token here and the login screen is skipped.
# Make one from the repo root (signed with the key in the root .env):
#
#   dotnet user-jwts create --project backend --role "emergency:Admin" --name "Demo Admin"
#
# The token is built into the app, so after changing it rebuild: docker compose up --build frontend
VITE_API_TOKEN=
